---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/marsello-vs-yotpo-email-sms';
const title = "Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS: replacing messaging without breaking loyalty";
const desc = "A Shopify stack review after Yotpo messaging retirement, separating Marsello loyalty adoption from retained Yotpo review and reward services.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can Yotpo Email be the new destination?",
    "answer": "Its Email and SMS products were scheduled for retirement and the product endpoint reports decommissioning. Evaluate an available messaging destination."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does Marsello replace Yotpo Reviews?",
    "answer": "Do not assume so. Assess review collection and display separately from loyalty and messaging, including retained product identifiers and content permissions."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the main loyalty migration risk?",
    "answer": "Unreconciled balances and outstanding rewards can create conflicting customer entitlements. Verify import behavior and redemption ownership before launch."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS: replacing messaging without breaking loyalty</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">This is now a replacement and ownership decision. A store with Yotpo messaging history should decide whether it needs a new sender, a new loyalty ledger, or both. Those projects have different data and customer obligations.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <p><em>Source descriptions checked November 24, 2026. Proposed exercises below are not completed tests or merchant results.</em></p>
        <h2>Retirement changes the comparison</h2>
        <p>Yotpo’s <a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">migration announcement</a> scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025; the <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">product endpoint</a> reports decommissioning. This does not imply retirement of its Reviews or Loyalty products. An old promise of consolidating new email into Yotpo is no longer a sound buying premise.</p>
        <h2>What Marsello offers to evaluate</h2>
        <p>The <a href="https://apps.shopify.com/marsello">Marsello developer listing</a> advertises points, rewards, VIP tiers and marketing add-ons for ecommerce and POS. That makes it relevant to a store considering loyalty and messaging together. It does not demonstrate import compatibility with a particular Yotpo balance export, review library or historical permission record.</p>
        <h2>Separate three inventories</h2>
        <p>Record messaging assets and suppressions first; then review collection, product identifiers and display widgets; then loyalty members, balances, tiers and outstanding rewards. For each, mark retain, replace or unresolved. Keeping a review service while changing email does not require moving the reward ledger. Moving rewards should have its own reconciliation and customer communication plan.</p>
        <h2>Proposed exercise: a member holds an unused reward</h2>
        <p>This proposed exercise has not been executed here. Select an authorized test member with earned points and an issued but unused reward. Document what the destination can import and what happens to the old reward code. Confirm a redemption cannot be counted twice and that a partial return updates the right ledger. Resolve unsupported states before opening enrollment in a second program.</p>
        <h2>Keep review collection distinct from reward earn</h2>
        <p>A review request and a points-earned notification serve different jobs. Assign one owner to each and document whether review submission earns an incentive under the retained program. Do not infer that Marsello replaces a review collection or display tool. Product matching and permission to reuse customer content need their own checks before review material appears in campaigns.</p>
        <h2>Retail staff need a usable transition</h2>
        <p>If adopting Marsello for POS loyalty, rehearse member lookup, enrollment and reward explanation with the intended permissions. Explain which balance staff should trust during transition and where to send disputes. Avoid simultaneously inviting customers into two competing reward programs merely to compare email templates.</p>
        <h2>Costs and measurement</h2>
        <p>Compare the proposed Marsello package with the complete retained stack, including any review tool and replacement sender. Include reward migration, support and staff instruction. Separate reward liability and redemption cost from subscription fees. Neither review volume nor the percentage of retail orders is a universal threshold for choosing a vendor.</p>
        <h2>Release independent pieces deliberately</h2>
        <p>Rebuild welcome, recovery, postpurchase and winback ownership without relying on a retired sender as rollback. Confirm what historical exports remain accessible. Preserve suppressions and channel-specific permission evidence, then verify links, coupons and pending messages. A loyalty launch can follow a messaging replacement once balances and terms are reconciled; forced same-day consolidation adds dependencies without proving value.</p>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/marsello-vs-klaviyo">Marsello vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-yotpo-email-sms">Klaviyo vs Yotpo Email & SMS</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">Post-purchase playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Marsello vs Yotpo Email & SMS FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
